WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.105
A few numbers capture the impact.

00:00:02.185 --> 00:00:09.258
MeZO delivers up to a twelvefold reduction in
memory compared with Adam fine-tuning on OPT-thirteen-billion,

00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:11.642
using no more memory than inference.

00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:13.827
On a single eighty-gigabyte A100,

00:00:13.907 --> 00:00:20.384
it trains a thirty-billion-parameter model where
backpropagation fits only two-point-seven billion.

00:00:20.464 --> 00:00:25.218
It matches fine-tuning within about one percent on
seven of eleven tasks,

00:00:25.298 --> 00:00:29.920
and it roughly halves the GPU-hours needed at the
thirty-billion scale.
